nasa-de-acquisition pack: content licence
===========================================

This pack is derived from:
  NASA Digital Engineering Acquisition Framework Handbook (NASA-HDBK-1004A)
  NASA-HDBK-1004A, approved 2026-10-26
  NASA, Office NASA Chief Engineer

Source licence: Public Domain (US Government work, 17 U.S.C. 105);
APPROVED FOR PUBLIC RELEASE--DISTRIBUTION IS UNLIMITED
(tier 1; see ../../docs/SOURCE-VETTING.md).
No source-material download link is published (see ../../docs/LICENSING.md).

The source is a NASA Technical Handbook prepared by the United States
Government and is not subject to copyright protection in the United States
(17 U.S.C. 105). Public release is taken from the cover line on the vetted
PDF. No printed DOPSR case was found. The cover text layer carries no
copyright notice. The handbook states guidance. It does not by itself
impose binding requirements outside a contract, grant, or agreement that
invokes it.

Third-party caveat: the handbook names external standards and contract
clause families. Those works stay with their publishers. This pack names
them and describes, in original words, how the handbook invokes them. It
reproduces no third-party standard text, no contract clause text, no DRD
template fields, and no selection-matrix rows cell by cell.

Attribution to NASA is a courtesy, not a legal obligation (see the
repository NOTICE). NASA does not endorse this pack or its authors.

NOTE: this file governs the CONTENT of the pack. The repository tooling is
licensed separately under MIT (see ../../LICENSE).
